Version 2.0.

The Windows sandbox implementation under `src/` is a vendored and adapted
subset of `codex-rs/windows-sandbox-rs` from openai/codex. The macOS Seatbelt
policy generator is a vendored and adapted subset of
`codex-rs/sandboxing/src/seatbelt.rs` plus its SBPL policy files.

Vendored from openai/codex at commit
5d89ab65dc9d4d0c55796c11df112b54157922b4. See SYNCING.md for how upstream
changes are tracked and re-applied.

The `gemini` Windows backend in `src/gemini.rs` is a Rust port of the core
token and Mandatory Integrity Control flow in Google Gemini CLI's
`GeminiSandbox.cs`, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0, at commit
ac42fb0a24fe7349e9968e2359ef5232f1cb6e72
(https://github.com/google-gemini/gemini-cli).

Modifications from upstream:
  * Retained the upstream Windows elevated setup helper, command runner,
    dedicated sandbox identities, DPAPI state, deny-read ACL handling, ConPTY,
    firewall/WFP rules, and helper materialization/package layout.
  * Replaced Codex-wide protocol/config types with a small serializable resolved
    permissions adapter shared by the main process and command runner.
  * Removed Codex OTEL/Statsig reporting while retaining setup logging and the
    underlying WFP/firewall behavior.
  * Kept the standalone synchronous capture API and the existing non-elevated
    supervisor, including bounded timeout/cancellation and optional live output.
  * Added a local windows-sys Job Object and ConPTY handle adapter instead of
    depending on Codex's general PTY crate.
  * Kept the macOS Seatbelt generator on local lightweight permission and
    absolute-path types.
  * Added the standalone `yj-sandbox-run` CLI with current Codex sandbox option
    names and `windows.sandbox = "gemini" | "elevated" | "unelevated"`
    selection. The local `gemini` mode is the default and supports multiple
    resolved writable roots.

